        "raw": "<p>This might be the first one-shot I completed with all heroes at full hit points.&nbsp; It was all over before the end of round 5.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Early on, I concentrated on giving Guise lots of extra powers to get lots of gift cards in play.&nbsp; In fact, by Guise’s turn on round 1, he let Legacy “open” 3 gift cards.&nbsp; In later rounds Guise let Parse open 4 gift cards and then next round open 5 gift cards himself.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>By that time the heroes were fully set up and shut Plague Rat down hard.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Had one surprising result.&nbsp; Mr. Fixer played “Grease Gun” to cancel out all non-hero damage.&nbsp; Guise on his turn played “Lemme See That!” (From opening his gift cards), so Guise took “Grease Gun” (not wanting to take Mr. Fixer’s “Pipe Wrench”).&nbsp; Here’s the neat thing: at the start of Mr. Fixer’s next turn, “Grease Gun” did NOT get discarded, since technically it was in Guise’s play area.&nbsp; On Guise’s turn “Grease Gun” moved back to Mr. Fixer’s play area.&nbsp; Net effect: the heroes got two rounds of no damage from one play of “Grease Gun”.&nbsp; I just sorta accidentally stumbled into this.&nbsp; After many (many, many, many) games of SotMV, I am still finding new tactics.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Good fun game.&nbsp; Every hero played their part.</p>",
